    <text type="letter">
        <body>
            <div type="writingSession">
                <pb n="1"/>
                <opener><dateline><date when="1948-07-14">July 14, 1948</date></dateline>
                    <salute>Dear <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928" type="person">Dr.
                        Tillich</rs>:</salute></opener>
                <p>This is just to let you know that materials for the first fall issue of the
                    Westminster Bookman are due in this office <date when="1948-07-26">July
                        26</date>, and we are wondering if we can expect to receive the article on
                        <rs ref="#tillich__U3DQJSPI" type="work">THE DEFINITION OF GOOD</rs>, by <rs
                        ref="#tillich_person_id__5319" type="person">A. C. Ewing</rs>, which we sent
                    you some time ago. We should like very much to have it then since the book has
                    been out now for some time, and if your schedule will permit you to do it by
                    then we shall appreciate it very much. If it will not be possible for you to do
                    it, will you let us know so we can complete our plans for that issue of the
                    Bookman?</p>
                <closer><salute>Sincerely yours,</salute><signed><hi rend="hand"><rs
                                ref="#tillich_person_id__5318" type="person">(Mrs.) Kathryn E.
                                Wagner</rs></hi><lb/><rs ref="#tillich_person_id__5318"
                            type="person">Kathryn E. Wagner</rs><lb/>RELIGIOUS BOOK
                        DEPARTMENT</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
